{
  "summary": "Guard against a null `CCoinControl` pointer in the `AvailableCoins` TRUC transaction filter, and expand fuzz test coverage to exercise unconfirmed mempool outputs with optional coin control.",
  "problem": "`AvailableCoins()` accepts an optional `CCoinControl` pointer that defaults to `nullptr`. A TRUC version filter dereferences the pointer unconditionally when evaluating unconfirmed outputs in the mempool, leading to a null pointer dereference if invoked without coin control.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The TRUC version filter added in ec2676becdf488f7a1151345a019c05dec926308 does not [check for null], so a call without coin control dereferences a null pointer as soon as the wallet has an unconfirmed output in the mempool.'",
    "Commit 6a5577f100 notes that production callers are currently safe: 'No current caller hits this: RPCs, the GUI and CreateTransaction always pass a coin control, and the tests and benchmarks that use the default only have confirmed coins.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The patch is small (+31/-2) and includes a wallet unit test and an update to the wallet spend fuzz target.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "This pull request adds a null check to the TRUC version filter in AvailableCoins and adds coverage in the wallet spend fuzz target. AvailableCoins defaults its coin control argument to null, but the TRUC filter dereferenced it unconditionally when checking unconfirmed mempool coins, causing a crash. While existing production RPC and GUI call sites pass an explicit coin control object, direct callers using the default argument would crash. The bug was detected via fuzzing.",
